from pathlib import Path
import shutil

root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]
fig=root/'figures/chapter3'
p=root/'Chapter3_results.md'
s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
old=next(x for x in s.split('\n') if x.startswith('The shared sets withstood'))
new='''Most shared enrichments persisted across the available sensitivity analyses. Forty-five of the 46 shared sets had the same enrichment direction in both HT1080 sampling periods; the exception, rRNA processing, was not significant in HT1080. Of the 16 shared sets significant in DU145, 15 remained significant after excluding genes flagged by the copy-number screen; the remaining set had an adjusted P value of 0.058 ([supplementary gene-set figure](figures/chapter3/ch03_supp_crossline_gene_sets.pdf)).

We next assessed the stability of inferred transcription-factor activity using multiple scoring methods, alternative target annotations and sample- and target-exclusion checks. Twenty-eight regulators in HT1080, three in A549 and eight in DU145 passed all six criteria. Lower STAT1- and MYC-associated scores passed in both HT1080 and DU145, whereas the lower JUN and NF-\u03baB scores in A549 did not survive the sample-omission and cross-method criteria. No regulator passed all six criteria in all three backgrounds ([TF comparison, panels a and b](figures/chapter3/ch03_main_crossline_tf_regulators.pdf)).

Shared-target analysis grouped 27 HT1080 regulators into one broad module, while A549 contained an HNF1A/HNF1B/FOXA2 group, with FOXA2 meeting the supported tier. DU145 contained three groups, of which only NFKB1/HBP1/RELA/NFKB met the module-stability threshold ([panel c](figures/chapter3/ch03_main_crossline_tf_regulators.pdf); [HT1080](figures/chapter3/ch03_supp_ht1080_tf_regulator_modules.pdf), [A549](figures/chapter3/ch03_supp_a549_tf_regulator_modules.pdf) and [DU145](figures/chapter3/ch03_supp_du145_tf_regulator_modules.pdf) supplementary figures, panels a\u2013c). The DU145 module's target-union score was no longer significant after excluding interferon-gamma or TNF/NF-\u03baB gene-set members, linking it to the immune-associated expression pattern. Correlation-aware fry tests gave a nominal P value of 0.023 for the HT1080 module and 0.078\u20130.172 for the A549 and DU145 modules ([sensitivity figure, panels a and b](figures/chapter3/ch03_supp_crossline_tf_module_sensitivity.pdf)). These results identify stable, overlapping target-expression patterns without directly establishing changes in regulator activity.

[![Inferred regulator scores and module stability across three cell backgrounds.](figures/chapter3/ch03_main_crossline_tf_regulators.png)](figures/chapter3/ch03_main_crossline_tf_regulators.pdf)

[Figure caption](Chapter3_figure_captions.md#main---inferred-regulator-patterns-vary-across-cell-backgrounds)'''
s=s.replace(old,new)
old=next(x for x in s.split('\n') if x.startswith('To identify candidate regulators, we inferred'))
s=s.replace(old,'''To identify candidate regulators, we scored expression patterns of annotated CollecTRI targets and tested their stability across methods, target annotations and sample exclusions. Twenty-eight regulators passed all six criteria, all with lower inferred activity. Twenty-seven shared a broad target-expression module, with contributing genes including MMP1, SPP1, MMP2, CXCL8 and SERPINE1 ([supplementary TF figure, panels a\u2013c](figures/chapter3/ch03_supp_ht1080_tf_regulator_modules.pdf)). These overlapping target patterns provide candidates for comparison with chromatin-accessibility evidence; they do not establish independent changes in each regulator's activity. The cross-line comparison and statistical sensitivity are described in Section 3.4.6.4.''')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')

captions={
'ch03_main_crossline_tf_regulators':('main - Inferred regulator patterns vary across cell backgrounds',
'''**Inferred regulator patterns vary across cell backgrounds.** a, CollecTRI ULM scores based on moderated t statistics for regulators passing all six checks in at least one background, plus FOXA2 and GRHL2. Blue and red indicate lower and higher scores in Y-depleted cells; filled and open circles identify robust and supported tiers. STAT1 and MYC pass all six checks in two backgrounds. b, Numbers of regulators at overall ULM FDR <0.05, divided by tier; labels give significant/tested counts. c, Module stability across 1,000 gene bootstraps and 200 resamples removing 20% of regulatory edges. Shading marks mean Jaccard similarity \u22650.75; both tests must meet this threshold. Asterisks identify modules below it. Columns give unadjusted fry P values for signed module-target unions and regulator membership/direction. Robust tiers require all six checks; supported tiers require R1 and R2 plus three of R3\u2013R6 (Methods). Period and omission checks differ with sampling design and measure within-population stability rather than independent editing replication.'''),
'ch03_supp_crossline_tf_module_sensitivity':('supp - Sensitivity of inferred regulator modules',
'''**Sensitivity of inferred regulator modules.** a, Empirical P values for regulator counts, clustering separation, target overlap and residual coactivity. The dashed line marks P = 0.05. Regulator counts test R1 and R2, not the complete six-rule selection. Rewiring used 200 iterations; silhouette comparisons use the eligible subset (HT1080, 200; A549, 8; DU145, 108). Target-overlap and coactivity tests used 1,000 and 10,000 iterations. b, Signed module-target ULM scores after excluding members of each indicated gene set. Vertical lines show scores before exclusion; open red circles indicate loss of nominal significance. Positive scores denote agreement with inferred regulator directions, not necessarily higher target expression. Axes are scaled separately. Annotations give expression-matched permutation P values (10,000 iterations) and unadjusted fry P values for the complete target unions. These exploratory P values are not corrected across modules or sensitivity tests.''')}
for line in ['HT1080','A549','DU145']:
 stem=f'ch03_supp_{line.lower()}_tf_regulator_modules'
 title=f'supp - Inferred regulators and shared targets in {line}'
 extra={'HT1080':'The module contains 27 of 28 robust regulators; NFE2L2 remains unclustered.',
        'A549':'Clustering includes three robust regulators and supported FOXA2; NCOR1 remains unclustered.',
        'DU145':'Dashed outlines and asterisks identify modules 2 and 3, which fall below the stability threshold.'}[line]
 captions[stem]=(title,f'''**Inferred regulators and shared targets in {line}.** a, ULM scores, regulator-wide BH FDR and robustness checks for robust (bold) and supported regulators. Filled/open circles indicate passed/failed checks. R1, ULM FDR <0.05; R2, direction agreement across periods or omissions; R3, agreement among at least three scoring methods; R4, direction agreement across available alternative priors; R5, direction agreement in leave-out refits; R6, retained direction and nominal significance after excluding self-edges and the three strongest contributing targets. See Methods for line-specific checks. b, Weighted overlap of leading target contributions; outlines identify modules. {extra} c, Contributing target genes ranked by summed contribution, with their moderated t statistics. Blue and red indicate lower and higher scores or expression, respectively. Module numbers correspond across panels; blank module entries indicate no assignment. These RNA-based scores do not directly measure regulator activity.''')
cp=root/'Chapter3_figure_captions.md'; text=cp.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
for stem,(title,caption) in captions.items():
 text+=f'\n\n## {title}\n\nFile: `figures/chapter3/{stem}.pdf`\n\n{caption}\n'
 anchor=title.lower().replace(' ','-')
 (fig/f'{stem}_notes.md').write_text(f'# {title}\n\nRetained for Chapter 3; coded selected-folder packaging remains pending.\n\nActive caption: [central captions](../../Chapter3_figure_captions.md#{anchor}).\n\nReproduce: `python SEPT_11_2026_THESIS/figures/chapter3/code/revise_tf_module_figures.py`. Saved analysis tables are read without refitting. Module fry values are unadjusted P values, not FDRs. Source tables and hashes accompany exports in `source_data/`.\n',encoding='utf-8')
cp.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
mp=root/'Chapter3_methods.md'; m=mp.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
needle='CollecTRI ULM activity inference used model log-fold changes, excluded conflicting duplicated regulatory edges and required at least five represented targets. BH correction spanned the tested regulators within each contrast. Inferred activity was considered directionally consistent when overall FDR was <0.05 and score directions agreed across periods. These target-pattern tests did not measure TF expression or occupancy.'
m=m.replace(needle,'Earlier descriptive CollecTRI scores used model log-fold changes. The regulator stability analysis below uses moderated t statistics and supersedes those scores for cross-line TF interpretation.')
m+='''\n\n### Transcription-factor score stability and shared-target modules

Saved moderated t statistics were scored using CollecTRI and decoupleR ULM, MLM, normalised weighted sums (1,000 permutations; seed 42) and VIPER, with at least five represented targets. ULM P values were BH-corrected across regulators within each contrast. Alternative-prior checks used DoRothEA A\u2013C and TFActProfiler all-tissue targets; the fibroblast prior was scored separately. Missing alternative-prior coverage did not count as disagreement. Six criteria defined the robust tier: overall ULM FDR <0.05 (R1); direction agreement across sampling units (R2); same direction and nominal P <0.05 for at least three of four methods (R3); agreement across available alternative priors (R4); same direction in all leave-out refits (R5); and retained direction and nominal P <0.05 after removing self-edges, complex-subunit self-edges and the three strongest contributing targets (R6). Supported regulators passed R1, R2 and at least three of R3\u2013R6. Correlation-aware fry tests were reported separately and were not tier-selection criteria.

For HT1080, R2 compared the two sampling periods and R5 omitted each of six passage pairs. A549 used eight single-library omissions of descriptive expression differences for R2 and eight unpaired-model refits for R5. DU145 used three passage-pair differences for R2 and three paired-model leave-one-pair-out refits for R5. A549 omission criteria are correlated; none of these checks establishes replication across independently edited populations.

Module nodes comprised robust regulators when at least eight were available, otherwise robust plus supported regulators. Leading targets comprised positive direction-aligned contributions accounting for 80% of their total. Weighted overlap was clustered by average linkage, choosing the partition with the highest mean silhouette; singletons were not reported as modules. Stability was evaluated by 1,000 gene bootstraps and 200 resamples dropping 20% of regulatory edges; mean best-match Jaccard similarity had to reach 0.75 in both. Structure checks compared R1/R2 counts and silhouette values with rewired networks, target overlap with size-matched regulator sets, and residual coactivity with permuted module labels. Only eligible rewired networks contributed silhouette values. Target unions used direction-aligned regulatory weights, expression-matched permutations and fry; positive scores therefore indicate agreement with inferred regulator directions. Module P values shown in figures are unadjusted. Gene-set exclusion tests removed indicated Hallmark or immediate-early genes and repeated target-union ULM scoring. No primary gene-level expression model was changed for these displays.
'''
mp.write_text(m,encoding='utf-8')
# Remove superseded main-labelled copies from the active directory after verified archival.
